Slack Interactivity requests (block_actions, view_submission, view_closed) reached the shared slackbot application source but were rejected, because the source only parsed Events API JSON. The source now verifies form-encoded interactivity bodies with the same signature check, decodes the payload field, routes by app and workspace, and normalizes interactions with trigger_id as the delivery id. Message event payloads stay unchanged to keep the shared conformance contract; the new event types are opt-in on sources and consumers. Tests cover routing, normalization, dedupe identity, rejections and Events API compatibility.
